---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FilmCard from '../components/FilmCard.astro';
import OperationsLoop from '../components/OperationsLoop.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  page="home"
  title="dmfdeploy — A shared foundation for dynamic media"
  description="An open, community-governed foundation for software-defined broadcast and media facilities. Explore the prototype, architecture and founding support programme."
>
  <section class="home-hero gradient-field" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Independent open infrastructure / Broadcast &amp; media</p>
          <h1 class="hero-title" id="home-title"><span>A shared </span><span>foundation </span><span>for dynamic </span><span>media.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-summary">An open, vendor-neutral foundation for declaring intent, deploying workloads and observing media facilities.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href="#architecture">Explore the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/dmfdeploy/dmfdeploy/blob/main/docs/THESIS.md">Read the thesis <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <FilmCard />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="project" aria-labelledby="project-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="problem-layout">
        <div>
          <p class="section-index">01 / Why this exists</p>
          <h2 class="problem-title" id="project-title">Media facilities can be <em>more adaptable.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="problem-copy">
          <p>Media engineering is moving from fixed appliances to software, IP and commodity compute. Deployment, inventory and operational visibility remain fragmented.</p>
          <p>dmfdeploy explores a shared foundation for declaring intent, deploying workloads and observing facility state.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="architecture-intro">
        <div><p class="section-index">02 / Architecture</p><h2 class="section-heading" id="architecture-title">A continuous operations loop.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-intro">Operations, automation, facility state and observation form the intended loop. The prototype demonstrates a narrower single-node path.</p>
      </div>
      <OperationsLoop />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="standards" aria-labelledby="standards-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="standards-head">
        <div><p class="section-index">03 / Standards &amp; tools</p><h2 class="section-heading" id="standards-title">Built in the open.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-intro">Open tools support the demonstrated deployment and observation path.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="standard-list">
        <article class="standard-card"><span class="eyebrow">Reference vocabulary</span><h3>EBU Dynamic Media Facility</h3><p>DMF concepts help frame the facility model. dmfdeploy is an independent initiative, not an EBU product or endorsement.</p></article>
        <article class="standard-card standard-card--pending"><span class="eyebrow">Next development step</span><h3>AMWA NMOS</h3><p>IS-05 controlled workload switching is a v0.2 target. It is not an implemented v0.1 capability.</p></article>
        <article class="standard-card standard-card--pending"><span class="eyebrow">Active experiment</span><h3>Media eXchange Layer</h3><p>MXL is being explored for media transport. The prototype does not claim a production media plane.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-rail" aria-label="Open-source tools in the prototype"><span>k3s</span><span>AWX</span><span>Helm</span><span>NetBox</span><span>Prometheus</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="status-head">
        <div><p class="section-index">04 / Project status</p><h2 class="section-heading" id="status-title">A working prototype. An open roadmap.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-intro">A demonstrated single-node path and a public roadmap for the work ahead.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="status-ledger">
        <article class="status-panel status-panel--observed"><span class="status-tag">First-party demonstrated</span><h3>In the prototype</h3><ul><li>Commodity ARM64, single-node facility path</li><li>Catalog intent to AWX, k3s and Helm execution</li><li>NetBox lifecycle and Prometheus target visibility</li><li>Operator console for the current control path</li></ul></article>
        <article class="status-panel status-panel--pending"><span class="status-tag status-tag--pending">Open development</span><h3>Next to prove</h3><ul><li>Independent cold-start reproduction of v0.1</li><li>Team console and NMOS IS-05 switching in v0.2</li><li>Workload and facility planning before provision in v0.3</li><li>Broader contributors and documented decision paths</li></ul></article>
      </div>
      <p class="status-disclaimer">The prototype is not a production ST 2110 or PTP facility. Multi-node operation, high availability and performance remain unverified.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="governance" aria-labelledby="governance-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="governance-grid">
        <div><p class="section-index">05 / Participation</p><h2 class="section-heading" id="governance-title">Technical direction belongs in the open.</h2></div>
        <div class="governance-copy"><p>Technical proposals move through public discussion, design records and reviewed contributions under Apache-2.0. Manufacturers, broadcasters and integrators can challenge assumptions and contribute integrations.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/dmfdeploy/dmfdeploy/discussions">Join the discussion <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sponsor-callout gradient-field" aria-labelledby="sponsor-callout-title">
    <div class="site-container sponsor-callout-inner">
      <div><span class="small-label">Founding support / Programme proposed</span><h2 id="sponsor-callout-title">Help build the shared foundation.</h2><p>Founding sponsors can fund the open engineering and documentation needed to make the prototype repeatable and useful across the industry.</p></div>
      <a class="button" href="/sponsor">Explore sponsorship <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
